---
title: Kenya Medical Association Endorses Bill Llia, Citing Healthcare Record
publishedDate: 2026-05-12
source: Kenya Medical Association (KMA)
sourceUrl: https://example.com/kma-endorsement-bill
excerpt: The Kenya Medical Association has endorsed Dr. Bill Llia for Governor of Nairobi County, praising his two-decade track record in community health and his detailed healthcare platform.
---

NAIROBI — The Kenya Medical Association (KMA), the professional body representing over 5,000 medical practitioners nationwide, today endorsed Dr. Bill Llia for Governor of Nairobi County — praising him as "one of our own who has spent his career delivering care in the communities that need it most."

In a statement signed by KMA chairperson Dr. Faith Nyambura, the association highlighted Llia's two decades of community health service and what it called "the most comprehensive, actionable healthcare platform of any candidate in this race."

"Dr. Llia is not a politician who discovered healthcare during campaign season — he is a clinician who has spent 20 years treating patients, training community health workers, and fighting for better health outcomes in Nairobi's most neglected wards," the statement read. "His plan for a community health centre in every ward, combined with his commitment to ending drug stock-outs and achieving zero preventable maternal deaths, represents the kind of detailed, accountable governance that Kenya needs at the county level."

The endorsement specifically highlighted four commitments from Llia's healthcare platform:
- A fully equipped community health centre within 30 minutes of every resident, with a published 18-month delivery timeline
- A county drug procurement reform using real-time inventory tracking to eliminate stock-outs at all public health facilities
- A maternal health programme targeting zero preventable maternal deaths in county facilities within Llia's first term
- Quarterly health insurance enrollment drives in every ward, in partnership with the National Hospital Insurance Fund

"This endorsement carries the weight of medical professionals who have seen the state of healthcare in Nairobi County firsthand — the empty shelves, the overcrowded wards, the preventable deaths," Llia said in response. "I am deeply honoured by the KMA's trust, and I am committed to proving that their confidence is well placed. We will build a healthcare system that every family in Nairobi County can depend on."

The KMA endorsement is expected to carry significant weight with voters, particularly in urban and peri-urban areas where access to quality healthcare is consistently ranked as the top issue.

